# Material Design 3 UI/UX Guidelines for Flutter Development

## Core Principles

This project follows **Material Design 3 (Material You)** guidelines for all UI development. The app is designed primarily for mobile devices but must be responsive and work seamlessly on tablets and larger screens.

## Material Design 3 Requirements

### Theme Configuration
- **ALWAYS** use `useMaterial3: true` in ThemeData
- Use `ColorScheme.fromSeed()` for dynamic color theming
- Support both light and dark themes using `ThemeMode`
- Use Material Design 3 color tokens (primary, secondary, tertiary, error, surface, etc.)
- Reference: https://m3.material.io/styles/color/the-color-system/overview

### Typography
- Use Material Design 3 typography scale:
  - Display Large/Medium/Small for hero text
  - Headline Large/Medium/Small for section headers
  - Title Large/Medium/Small for card titles
  - Body Large/Medium/Small for content
  - Label Large/Medium/Small for buttons and labels
- Use `Theme.of(context).textTheme` instead of hardcoded text styles
- Ensure proper text contrast ratios (WCAG AA minimum)
- Reference: https://m3.material.io/styles/typography/overview

### Spacing & Layout
- Use Material Design 3 spacing tokens (4dp, 8dp, 16dp, 24dp, 32dp, 48dp, 64dp)
- Use `SizedBox` with multiples of 4dp for spacing
- Use `Padding` with EdgeInsets that follow the 4dp grid system
- For responsive layouts, use `LayoutBuilder` or `MediaQuery` to detect screen size
- Reference: https://m3.material.io/styles/layout/spacing

### Component Guidelines

#### Buttons
- Use Material 3 button styles:
  - `FilledButton` for primary actions
  - `OutlinedButton` for secondary actions
  - `TextButton` for tertiary actions
  - `IconButton` for icon-only actions
- Button height: minimum 40dp (mobile), 48dp (tablet)
- Button padding: horizontal 24dp, vertical 12dp
- Use `FloatingActionButton` with Material 3 styling for primary FABs
- Reference: https://m3.material.io/components/buttons/overview

#### Cards
- Use `Card` widget with Material 3 elevation (0dp, 1dp, 3dp, 5dp, 8dp)
- Card padding: 16dp (mobile), 24dp (tablet)
- Card corner radius: 12dp (small), 16dp (medium), 28dp (large)
- Use `Card.elevated` for elevated cards
- Reference: https://m3.material.io/components/cards/overview

#### Navigation
- Use Material 3 navigation components:
  - `NavigationBar` for bottom navigation (mobile)
  - `NavigationRail` for side navigation (tablet/desktop)
  - `NavigationDrawer` for drawer navigation
- Navigation bar height: 80dp
- Navigation rail width: 80dp (collapsed), 256dp (expanded)
- Use `AppBar` with Material 3 styling
- Reference: https://m3.material.io/components/navigation/overview

#### Text Fields
- Use `TextField` with Material 3 styling
- Use `OutlinedBorder` for outlined text fields
- Use `FilledBorder` for filled text fields
- Label text size: 12sp
- Input text size: 16sp
- Padding: 16dp horizontal, 12dp vertical
- Reference: https://m3.material.io/components/text-fields/overview

#### Dialogs
- Use `Dialog`, `AlertDialog`, or `showDialog` with Material 3 styling
- Dialog corner radius: 28dp
- Dialog padding: 24dp
- Use `Dialog` for full-screen dialogs on mobile, centered dialogs on tablet
- Reference: https://m3.material.io/components/dialogs/overview

#### Lists
- Use `ListTile` with Material 3 styling
- List item height: minimum 48dp (mobile), 56dp (tablet)
- Leading/trailing icon size: 24dp
- Use `Divider` with 1dp height for list separators
- Reference: https://m3.material.io/components/lists/overview

#### Chips
- Use `Chip`, `FilterChip`, `ChoiceChip`, `ActionChip`, or `InputChip`
- Chip height: 32dp
- Chip padding: 8dp horizontal, 4dp vertical
- Reference: https://m3.material.io/components/chips/overview

## Responsive Design Guidelines

### Breakpoints
- **Mobile**: < 600dp width
- **Tablet**: 600dp - 840dp width
- **Desktop**: > 840dp width

### Responsive Patterns

#### Layout Adaptation
```dart
// Use LayoutBuilder or MediaQuery for responsive layouts
LayoutBuilder(
  builder: (context, constraints) {
    if (constraints.maxWidth < 600) {
      // Mobile layout: single column, bottom navigation
      return MobileLayout();
    } else {
      // Tablet layout: multi-column, navigation rail
      return TabletLayout();
    }
  },
)
```

#### Adaptive Components
- **Mobile**: Use `NavigationBar` at bottom
- **Tablet**: Use `NavigationRail` on the left side
- **Mobile**: Use single-column layouts
- **Tablet**: Use multi-column layouts (2-3 columns)
- **Mobile**: Full-screen dialogs
- **Tablet**: Centered dialogs with max width constraints

#### Spacing Adaptation
- Mobile: Use tighter spacing (8dp, 16dp)
- Tablet: Use more generous spacing (16dp, 24dp, 32dp)
- Use `MediaQuery.of(context).size.width` to determine spacing

### Touch Targets
- Minimum touch target size: 48dp × 48dp (mobile), 40dp × 40dp (tablet)
- Ensure adequate spacing between interactive elements (8dp minimum)

## Accessibility Guidelines

### Color & Contrast
- Ensure text meets WCAG AA contrast ratios:
  - Normal text: 4.5:1 contrast ratio
  - Large text (18sp+): 3:1 contrast ratio
- Use `ColorScheme` colors that automatically provide proper contrast
- Test with both light and dark themes

### Screen Reader Support
- Always provide `semanticLabel` for icon-only buttons
- Use `Semantics` widget for custom widgets
- Ensure all interactive elements are focusable

### Text Scaling
- Use relative units (sp for text, dp for layout)
- Test with system font scaling (up to 200%)
- Avoid fixed pixel sizes for text

## Animation & Motion

### Material Motion
- Use Material 3 motion patterns:
  - Easing: `Curves.easeInOut` for most transitions
  - Duration: 200ms-300ms for most animations
  - Use `AnimatedContainer`, `AnimatedOpacity`, etc. for smooth transitions
- Reference: https://m3.material.io/styles/motion/overview

### Transitions
- Page transitions: Use Material 3 page transitions
- Dialog transitions: Use Material 3 dialog transitions
- List item animations: Use `AnimatedList` or `ListView` with `AnimatedList` for smooth insertions/deletions

## Code Examples

### Theme Setup
```dart
ThemeData(
  useMaterial3: true,
  colorScheme: ColorScheme.fromSeed(
    seedColor: Colors.blue,
    brightness: Brightness.light,
  ),
  // Use Material 3 typography
  textTheme: Typography.material2021().black,
)
```

### Responsive Button
```dart
FilledButton(
  style: FilledButton.styleFrom(
    padding: EdgeInsets.symmetric(
      horizontal: MediaQuery.of(context).size.width < 600 ? 16 : 24,
      vertical: 12,
    ),
    minimumSize: Size(
      0,
      MediaQuery.of(context).size.width < 600 ? 40 : 48,
    ),
  ),
  onPressed: () {},
  child: Text('Button'),
)
```

### Responsive Layout
```dart
LayoutBuilder(
  builder: (context, constraints) {
    final isTablet = constraints.maxWidth >= 600;
    return isTablet
        ? Row(
            children: [
              NavigationRail(...),
              Expanded(child: Content()),
            ],
          )
        : Column(
            children: [
              Expanded(child: Content()),
              NavigationBar(...),
            ],
          );
  },
)
```

